Kyðè¨T½ÊZvˆ°´Œ÷¶^ðlÈÍ¿a~–{"rendered":{"html":"<p>You can check a GCSL program without running its effects, then format its\nsource consistently. The checker and formatter deliberately have different\nscopes: checking needs workspace relationships; formatting only needs\nsource text that parses.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tools-checking-and-formatting--before-you-start\">Before you start <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#tools-checking-and-formatting--before-you-start\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>You need <code>gcsl</code> and an existing source file or workspace. Commit or save\nyour changes before rewriting files so you can review the formatting diff.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tools-checking-and-formatting--check-and-format\">Check and format <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#tools-checking-and-formatting--check-and-format\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Check a file, including its enclosing workspace if it has one:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\" data-copy-code><span class=\"copy-label\">Copy</span></button><pre><code><span class=\"hl-source hl-shell hl-bash\"><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-variable hl-function hl-shell\">gcsl</span></span><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell\"> check main.gcsl</span>\n</span></code></pre></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Preview whether formatting would change that file:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\" data-copy-code><span class=\"copy-label\">Copy</span></button><pre><code><span class=\"hl-source hl-shell hl-bash\"><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-variable hl-function hl-shell\">gcsl</span></span><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell\"> fmt<span class=\"hl-variable hl-parameter hl-option hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-punctuation hl-definition hl-parameter hl-shell\"> --</span>check</span> main.gcsl</span>\n</span></code></pre></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Apply the formatter and repeat the check:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\" data-language=\"sh\"><button class=\"copy-code\" type=\"button\" data-copy-code><span class=\"copy-label\">Copy</span></button><pre><code><span class=\"hl-source hl-shell hl-bash\"><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-variable hl-function hl-shell\">gcsl</span></span><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell\"> fmt main.gcsl</span>\n<span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-variable hl-function hl-shell\">gcsl</span></span><span class=\"hl-meta hl-function-call hl-arguments hl-shell\"> fmt<span class=\"hl-variable hl-parameter hl-option hl-shell\"><span class=\"hl-punctuation hl-definition hl-parameter hl-shell\"> --</span>check</span> main.gcsl</span>\n</span></code></pre></div>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"tools-checking-and-formatting--check-the-result\">Check the result <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#tools-checking-and-formatting--check-the-result\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The checker reports its summary on standard error. Warnings alone do not\nmake it fail. The final formatting check succeeds without listing the\nfile when it is already formatted.</p>\n<p>A file with lexical or syntax errors is left untouched by the formatter;\nfix those diagnostics and retry. Formatting does not require a successful\ntype check. It uses one language style rather than editor-specific indent\nsettings.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tools-checking-and-formatting--checking-a-tree\">Checking a tree <a class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#tools-checking-and-formatting--checking-a-tree\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>\n<p>With no paths, both commands use the enclosing workspace and exclude\nnested workspaces. An explicit directory makes them discover nested\nworkspaces too. However, <code>gcsl check DIRECTORY</code> checks workspaces, not\nunattached <code>.gcsl</code> files under that directory. Pass each standalone file\nexplicitly when it also needs checking.</p>\n<p>For automation, <code>gcsl check --message-format json main.gcsl</code> writes one\nJSON diagnostic per line to standard output and keeps the summary on\nstandard error. See <code>gcsl(1)</code> for the schema and exit statuses.</p>\n","toc":[{"level":2,"id":"tools-checking-and-formatting--before-you-start","title":"Before you start","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"tools-checking-and-formatting--check-and-format","title":"Check and format","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"tools-checking-and-formatting--check-the-result","title":"Check the result","number":null},{"level":2,"id":"tools-checking-and-formatting--checking-a-tree","title":"Checking a tree","number":null}],"has_mermaid":false,"dangling":[],"warnings":[],"broken":[]},"images":[],"links":{"pages":[],"anchors":[]},"refs":null}